# Alembic Schema Provenance

This directory is the temporary schema source of truth for the new Go/Svelte
Conbench runtime while it runs on the frozen production Postgres schema.

The active server, CLI, web app, and Python SDK do not import these files at
runtime. Schema generation runs them inside the isolated schema image from
`Dockerfile.schema` with `requirements-schema.txt`. The schema image does not
import the retired Python client packages and does not import the retired Flask
application.

Use the Make targets instead of invoking Alembic directly:

```bash
make schema
make schema-check
ALEMBIC_MIGRATION_NAME=describe_change make schema-new-migration
```

`make schema` regenerates `internal/db/schema.sql`, which is the checked sqlc
input consumed by the Go backend. `make schema-check` verifies that checked-in
SQL still matches these migrations.

Retire this directory when schema ownership moves out of the legacy
Python/Alembic path. Until then, keep migrations limited to schema provenance
and schema drift checks; do not add runtime Python application code here.
